# GitHub Repository Management

### Repository Creation

Create a repository on GitHub and connect it with the local repository.

```bash
git remote add origin <repository-url>
git push -u origin main
```

### Teams & Permissions

GitHub allows team members to have different access levels such as **Read, Write, Maintain, and Admin**.

### Branch Protection

Branch rules can prevent direct pushes and require pull requests or reviews before merging.

### CODEOWNERS

`CODEOWNERS` defines which users or teams are responsible for specific files.

Example:

```text
/docs/ @team-name
```

